      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="1205934232">
          <groundspeak:date>2023-11-17T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="25790230">MaybeSunshine</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP666 Ranchlands [FOUND]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fortunately for me (because grass had completely grown over the cap now), DanOCan’s photo from 2015 was so helpful that I was able to match rocks and find it fairly easily tonight, even in the dark with no equipment. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684223381">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="3061435">Iron Phoenix</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP666 - Ranchlands&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Out for another day of capping and caching with OBA, picking up ones we didn't get to earlier! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; A busy day today and lots of walking, but a lot of fun!! &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_big.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; I swear I've been to this cap before... my best friend lives nearby and I thought we had gone for a walk to find this once.  Maybe just a Traditional nearby. &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_blackeye.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; Oh well, found it today and the geodog loved her walk in the park!! TFTCap!!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683868787">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="2034047">Cachin8r</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP666 Ranchlands&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ninth of 12 caches today, #866. It was just me and a friend for the last four caps of the day (starting with this one). It was a spontaneous decision to meet him but he was on board with searching caps with me. I scrapped the last bit of my route and chose some closer to his house. This one blended in pretty well. Good location for a cap and a nice view too. Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;-Cachin&lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile_8ball.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt;r&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="683848074">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-03T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP666 - Ranchlands - oh the views are lovely from up here!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Iron Phoenix and I spent the day continuing our Calgary and area capping spree. Thanks for the work you do maintaining the caps outforthehunt.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
